From c82545eae4ffa58ef1961eb2034e4a2b46f4f1a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gris Ge <fge@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Feb 2026 13:48:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ip: Allow ignoring IP address with other protocol

Introduce a query-only `protocol` property for IP addresses. Addresses
with an "other" (non-kernel) protocol are assigned by external tools
like OVN and must not be persisted into NM configuration, so ignore
them in desired state and when preserving addresses during route
changes.

Resolves: https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RHEL-243331

Signed-off-by: Gris Ge <fge@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Josephine Pfeiffer <josie@redhat.com>

Resolved Conflicts:
  rust/src/lib/ip.rs
  rust/src/lib/unit_tests/ip.rs

(cherry picked from commit 3bbac32aa342409d575060667e2cb6dd26c9ba7e)
